    "Selling AI solutions to traditional local business owners requires a completely different approach than selling to tech-savvy online startups. Local service business owners?contractors, doctors, attorneys, and automotive repair managers?are bombarded with unsolicited cold calls from marketing agencies promising search engine optimization, Facebook ads, and social media management. They are skeptical, busy, and naturally protective of their time.",
    "If you approach a local business owner using complex technical jargon?talking about vector databases, large language models, prompt engineering, or RAG architecture?their eyes will glaze over, and they will immediately show you the door. They do not care about technology; they care about Three Things: New Revenue, Lower Overhead, and Peace of Mind.",
